y 21st is  what here somewhere and up until June  21st which is today that's not quite  noon filming this yet so I can't mark it  off but that really helped just kind of  stay on track and you'd like to see the  progress and when you see those X's  coming on you don't want to break the  chain and so you want to keep going  every day wait number 4 was a used  Saturday as a cheat day and that was  when I could eat whatever I wanted you  know there was no calorie restriction  that just ate ate ate ate ate ate ate  but I still had to keep my chain so I  still was running for 30 minutes in the  day and I was still fasting until noon  this was one of the hardest things  because I get this delicious doughnut  from Tim Hortons or this breakfast that  ends at noon and so I really wanted to  eat dad so he buy it a couple minutes  early I'd be sitting there looking at my  doughnut like I got five minutes left  before I can eat this thing  and then once noon came but show it in  so Saturday is my cheat day  but I still am on my fast until noon  it's 15 minutes till noon and I'm  excited to dig into my Boston cream  doughnut this is gonna be a brutal 15  minutes I love it so that really helped  that helps it helps on a psychological  level to have one day when you can eat  whatever you want and I think there is  also a lot of research that backs up  having a cheat day to kind of spike your  levels and then come back down can  actually facilitate more weight loss as  well and so I found that really helpful  but I kept to my fasting until noon and  running 30 minutes a day guys when you  persevere and it's hard and you make it  through and you win the victory is just  so much sweeter  [Music]  we number five was no packaged foods and  so I made a decision apart from the  coffee that would have in the morning I  wouldn't need anything from a package so  nothing with a wrapper nothing  store-bought that was not just processed  but even healthy stuff I wouldn't eat  from a wrapper so